    >[ ] Add transaction request and result schemas with fixtures =transaction-schemas $Publish strict Draft 2020-12 schemas plus valid and invalid fixtures for ordered update-action, complete-action, and cancel-action operations and their dry-run, committed, or typed-failure result.$ !1 <index-json-contract #019fdffc-b169-7d32-95af-b3e73d0a1412
    >[ ] Validate producer bytes against the schemas =schema-producer-tests $Test graphd index output and CLI transaction results at their producer boundaries against one canonical schema source; do not make the query forwarding shim inspect payloads.$ !1 <transaction-schemas #019fdffc-b172-7153-a823-e9d67c81f18e
[ ] Restore transparent graphd queries through clearhead =query-facade ~ $Reintroduce clearhead query as an inherited-stdio process facade over graphd, preserving graphd bytes, rendering, and exit behavior while keeping all graph logic in graphd.$ !1 #019fdffc-b17c-7833-bb3e-34c5d4480901
    >[ ] Restore forwarding for current graphd query families and formats =query-forwarding $Recover the former shim as implementation history, update it for current raw, named, index, tree, graph, list, and show commands and current formats, and retain fuzzy chain resolution only as a canonical-ID adapter.$ !1 #019fdffc-b18d-7d81-8dca-fb88f818a0cf
    >[ ] Prove query output feeds existing CLI verbs unchanged =query-to-verb $Use real graphd index JSON, select an urn:uuid identity, and pass it directly to show and a safe mutation dry-run; assert forwarded stdout and exit status match direct graphd execution.$ !1 <query-forwarding #019fdffc-b196-7e10-adb1-aed7338db159
[ ] Implement the minimal atomic action transaction =action-transaction ~ $Plan a small ordered batch of action update, complete, and cancel operations against trusted current state and commit all affected files through one existing PendingBatch.$ !1 <workflow-schemas #019fdffc-b19f-7062-871f-d1220e0e546c
    >[ ] Define typed update complete and cancel operations =action-transaction-types $Deserialize the published tagged operation shapes, normalize canonical IDs, and apply them in order to an in-memory trusted workspace model without adding plans, charters, move, delete, generic JSON Patch, or snapshot revisions.$ !1 #019fdffc-b1b0-7681-9dc2-6a57ae571db7
    >[ ] Reject an invalid batch before any write =action-transaction-plan $Resolve every target and validate every transition plus the resulting state under the workspace lock; return one deterministic plan or one typed failure, with dry-run stopping before staging.$ !1 <action-transaction-types #019fdffc-b1b8-7360-9d7a-4c8e3e2b8b4e
    >[ ] Commit all affected action files and sidecars once =action-transaction-commit $Render the approved in-memory result, stage each changed active file, completed file, and sidecar in one existing PendingBatch, commit once, and prove interrupted commits recover without lost or duplicated actions.$ !1 <action-transaction-plan #019fdffc-b1c2-7c73-b862-4475695a8e1d
[ ] Expose and dogfood the complete data workflow =transact-workflow ~ $Add clearhead transact for stdin or a request file, emit the minimal schema-valid result, and prove query data can be selected and atomically acted on through ordinary shell composition.$ !2 <query-facade <action-transaction #019fdffc-b1cb-7f80-99d4-ce37de3bd899
    >[ ] Add clearhead transact with file stdin and dry-run input =transact-command $Schema-validate JSON before typed decoding, invoke the Core planner and committer, keep diagnostics off machine stdout, and emit only the compact committed, dry-run, or typed-failure result.$ !2 #019fdffc-b1dc-76c3-8865-784c94a3d00f
    >[ ] Prove query to jq to transact to query end to end =transact-loop-e2e $Through the real binaries, query an index as JSON, transform selected canonical IDs into a multi-operation request, apply or dry-run it, re-query, and verify invalid batches write nothing.$ !2 <transact-command #019fdffc-b1e6-7c31-ab82-80efb7e79df4
    >[ ] Document the simple composition contract and close the charter =transact-workflow-docs $Publish schemas and concise human and agent examples, record the narrow restoration of the CLI facade, state the intentionally deferred complexity, run focused Core CLI graphd and doctor checks, and close when the charter done gate is evidenced.$ !2 <transact-loop-e2e #019fdffc-b1ef-7952-bcca-032e9a1300de
